WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:04.140
With Avengers: Infinity War fast approaching,
fans are getting totally geeked up at the

00:00:04.140 --> 00:00:08.180
promise of finally seeing the heroes of the
Marvel Cinematic Universe face off against

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:09.580
the ultimate evil, Thanos.

00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:13.820
But once the wrinkly, purple Titan is presumably
defeated, who will the next big bad guy be

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:14.640
in the MCU?

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:19.360
Well, no one really knows, but we do know
who it won't be, thanks to complex licensing

00:00:19.360 --> 00:00:19.860
issues.

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.860
Here's a look at some villains Marvel can't
use in their movies.

00:00:23.660 --> 00:00:24.480
Galactus

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:30.080
If there's one villain who's bigger than Thanos
both literally and figuratively, it's Galactus,

00:00:30.080 --> 00:00:34.500
a planet devouring force of nature born before
the Big Bang even created our universe.

00:00:34.760 --> 00:00:37.620
In the comics, he's pretty much the ultimate
unbeatable power.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:40.900
In the world of movies, however, his rights
belong to Fox.

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:47.020
The result is one incredibly boring and disappointing
cameo as an angry cloud in Fantastic Four:

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.060
Rise of the Silver Surfer.

00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:53.350
Galactus would be amazing in the MCU, but
for now, he's stuck in bad-movie limbo with

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.740
the rest of the Fantastic Four.

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:57.760
"I am Galactus.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:02.380
The be-all and end-all of the universe."

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.020
Dr. Doom

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.620
Like Galactus, Dr. Doom's rights are tied
up with the Fantastic Four.

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:12.080
Unlike Galactus, though, Doom may actually
be resilient enough to break free of the Fantastic

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:14.000
Four's legacy of crappy movies.

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:18.460
Though versions of the bad doctor have already
appeared in every Fantastic Four film through

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:24.420
2017, it was recently revealed that Fox is
developing a stand-alone Dr. Doom solo film.

00:01:24.640 --> 00:01:28.260
That sounds promising, but it also means we
won't be seeing Doom take on the Avengers

00:01:28.260 --> 00:01:29.920
in the MCU any time soon.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.560
"I would like a word with you, Stark"

00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:37.060
Magneto

00:01:37.740 --> 00:01:41.120
Fox has had a pretty spotty track record with
their superhero films, but one thing they've

00:01:41.130 --> 00:01:45.290
totally nailed is the character of Magneto,
who's been expertly played by both Ian McKellen

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:47.520
and Michael Fassbender over the past two decades.

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:51.660
In the comics, Magneto has frequently branched
out from the world of mutants to battle heroes

00:01:51.660 --> 00:01:52.580
like the Avengers.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:57.040
But as long as the X-Men films remain profitable,
there's no chance Fox will let Magneto's rights

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:00.780
revert to Marvel Studios, as the character
is a cornerstone of the franchise.

00:02:00.940 --> 00:02:04.360
Which is too bad, because it would be cool
to see them try to reconcile the two different

00:02:04.360 --> 00:02:05.660
versions of Magneto's children.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:07.200
Venom

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.160
Sony kept Venom off the big screen for years
following his underwhelming debut in Sam Raimi's

00:02:12.169 --> 00:02:17.409
Spider-Man 3, but he'll soon return in a standalone
feature starring Tom Hardy that's reportedly

00:02:17.409 --> 00:02:20.320
meant to launch the studio's own version of
the Marvel universe.

00:02:20.560 --> 00:02:23.820
Of course, exactly how this is going to work
now that Spider-Man himself is appearing in

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:28.390
the Marvel Cinematic Universe is still unclear,
so it's possible Venom could eventually cross

00:02:28.390 --> 00:02:32.559
over between universes, which would be cool,
considering Venom eventually ended up joining

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:34.459
the Guardians of the Galaxy in the comics.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:35.400
So, we'll see!

00:02:36.040 --> 00:02:37.240
Other Spidey villains

00:02:37.800 --> 00:02:41.590
If the fate of Venom is confusing, things
are even more unclear when it comes to the

00:02:41.590 --> 00:02:43.260
rest of Spidey's rogue's gallery.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.439
Sony reportedly is developing a film featuring
both Black Cat and Silver Sable, so it looks

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:49.420
like they're off the board.

00:02:49.689 --> 00:02:54.420
And once upon a time, Sony had plans to do
a Sinister Six film featuring a team-up between

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.220
villains like Electro, Doctor Octopus, and
Mysterio.

00:02:57.820 --> 00:03:02.640
However, Sinister Six member the Vulture already
appeared in the MCU, and the post-credits

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:06.999
teaser of Spider-Man: Homecoming hinted that
more members of the team — such as the Scorpion

00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:08.320
— may be joining him soon.

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:12.719
But until we hear otherwise, fans should assume
that all of Spidey's villains are off-limits

00:03:12.720 --> 00:03:13.940
when it comes to the MCU.

00:03:15.100 --> 00:03:15.720
Sabretooth

00:03:16.320 --> 00:03:21.920
At best, 2009's Wolverine: Origins was a missed
opportunity, squandering characters like Deadpool

00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:24.220
and Gambit in service of a truly joyless movie.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:29.790
At worst, Fox wasted a great performance by
Liev Schreiber as Sabretooth, who hasn't been

00:03:29.790 --> 00:03:31.209
seen in the X-Men films since.

00:03:31.209 --> 00:03:36.580
"The dream is over, and the best is awake."

00:03:36.900 --> 00:03:38.940
"My name is Victor Creed.

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:40.280
AHHHHHHH!"

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:44.900
The fact that Fox isn't actually using Sabretooth
makes it especially galling that Marvel can't

00:03:44.900 --> 00:03:48.340
use him in their films either, because there
are plenty of places where he could fit in.

00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:51.320
Wouldn't Sabretooth versus Black Panther blow
your mind?

00:03:51.660 --> 00:03:56.019
Alas, as long as Marvel doesn't own the film
rights, the best we can do is hope he pops

00:03:56.020 --> 00:03:57.100
up in another X-Men movie.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:03:59.080
Apocalypse

00:03:59.660 --> 00:04:03.740
As far as X-Men movies go, Apocalypse is a
relatively recent villain.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:07.900
And X-Men: Apocalypse was a pretty disappointing
showcase for the character considering what

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:09.980
a world-class threat he is in the comics.

00:04:10.280 --> 00:04:14.379
In one alternate universe storyline, Apocalypse
actually conquered the world and reshaped

00:04:14.380 --> 00:04:15.260
it in his own image.

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:19.419
That sounds like the perfect type of villain
to follow in Thanos's footsteps, giving the

00:04:19.420 --> 00:04:22.180
good guys of the MCU a real threat to fight
against.

00:04:22.460 --> 00:04:26.699
For now, however, like all of these other
great characters, Apocalypse is stuck in Fox's

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:31.500
hands thanks to the true enemy of Marvel superheroes:
bad business deals.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:32.660
Thanks for watching!

00:04:32.980 --> 00:04:35.360
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.980
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

